From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sarge <dan@19labs.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 07:55:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Moonraker client hardening for the lab Klipper printer

- Subscribe only to objects that expose get_status; configfile,
  gcode_macro *, secondary mcu nodes etc. made Klipper reject the whole
  subscription. Core telemetry objects are always kept.
- Stale-state watchdog, WebSocket keepalive and a 2 s HTTP state poll in
  the Moonraker client.
- File browser and controls panel list and start prints through
  /api/printers/:id/files for Moonraker-type printers, with HTML-escaped
  error text; matching server routes.
- Local lab patch on top of upstream v1.1.25; a copy is exported to
  vdroners/nc-print docs/patches/3dprintforge/.

Co-developed-by: Claude (model: claude-opus-4.7, context: 200k)
